# Readability First

This repo is revisited after long gaps — weeks, months, sometimes years.
Every file must be understandable cold, with no prior context.

## Core rules

- Prefer readable code over clever or compact code — always
- Prefer clarity over optimization — note optimizations in the docstring instead
- Write approach notes as if explaining to yourself after a long break
- Never omit steps in the approach notes because logic "seems obvious"
- No terse one-liners when a few clear lines communicate better
- If a trick or shortcut is used, explain it in a comment

## Variable naming

- Descriptive names always
- Single-letter names only for well-known patterns: `i`, `j` (loop counters), `left`/`right` (two pointers)
- No abbreviations that aren't immediately obvious

## The test

> "Could I re-read this file cold, after 6 months, and understand it immediately?"

If the answer is no — rewrite it.
